  "description": "The EPO is a US Made, Italian steel, road frame. Actually, it's 38c max tire clearance makes it an All-Road bike, right? Who knows anymore. Anyway...the EPO is built by Darren Larkin up in Connecticut in very small batches. It's made up of an assortment of the finest Columbus steel available. The fine Italian tubes provide a ride quality that will have you wanting to push this bike like you've been juiced up and are breaking away in the '99 Tour de France. Each frame comes paired up with an ENVE AR Disc Fork to match the frame's tire clearance and keep the front end light and nimble.\n\n!!IMPORTANT!! These are available either with OR without shifter cable guides for those of you devoted to the eTap. When selecting your frame size, if you want shift cable guides choose MECHANICAL, if you're running eTap for life then choose ETAP.\n\nDesigned around a 700c wheelset with a max tire size of 38c. You could set it up 650 as well and have around the same tire clearance.\n\nFlat Mount Brake Calipers front and rear\n\nFront and rear thru axles are included\n\nThis frame is not ED Coated and has not been treated internally. If you feel the need to do so, do it.\n\nMaximum amount of spacers on steerer 40mm (this does not include the stem)\n\nHEADSET NOT INCLUDED\n\nHandmade in USA by Darren Larkin\n\nTig Welded High End Columbus Steel Frame with Carbon Fork",
